.TH SIGACTION 2P "August 1, 1992"
.ds ]W POSIX 1003.1
.SH NAME
sigaction \- (POSIX only) examine or specify the action to be associated with a specific
signal.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <signal.h>
.sp
int sigaction(int \fIsig\fP, const struct sigaction *\fIact\fP, struct sigaction *\fIoact\fP)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The information in this specification applies
only to POSIX applications.
.PP
The \fIsigaction\fP function allows the calling process to examine or specify
(or both) the action to be associated with a specific signal.  The argument
\fIsig\fR specifies the signal.
.PP
If the argument \fIact\fR is not NULL, it points to a structure
specifying the action to be associated with the specified signal.
If the argument \fIoact\fR is not NULL, the action previously
associated with the signal is stored in the location pointed to by
the argument \fIoact\fR. If the argument \fIact\fR is NULL,
signal handling is unchanged by this function call.
.PP
The \fIsa_handler\fR field of the \fIsigaction\fR structure identifies
the action to be associated with the specified signal.  If the
\fIsa_handler\fR field specifies a signal-catching function, the
\fIsa_mask\fR field identifies a set of signals that shall be added
to the signal mask of the process before the signal-catching function
is invoked.  Ths SIGKILL and SIGSTOP signals shall not be added to
the signal mask using this mechanism.
.PP
The SA_NOCLDSTOP bit of the \fIsa_flags\fR field may be used to
modify the behavior of the specified signal.  If \fIsig\fR is
SIGCHLD and the SA_NOCLDSTOP flag is not set in \fIsa_flags\fR, a
SIGCHLD signal shall be generated for the calling process whenever
any of its child processes stop.
.PP
When a signal is caught by a signal-catching function installed by
the \fIsigaction\fR function, a new signal mask is calculated
and installed for the duration of the signal-catching function (or
until a call to either the \fIsigprocmask(2P)\fR or \fIsigsuspend(2P)\fR
function is made).  This mask is formed by taking the union of the
current signal mask and the value of the \fIsa_mask\fR for the
signal being delivered and then including the signal being delivered.
If and when the signal handler returns normally, the original signal
mask is restored.
.PP
Once an action is installed for a specific signal, it remains
installed until another action is explicitly requested (by another
call to the \fIsigaction\fR function) or until one of the
\fIexec(2)\fR functions is called.
.SH RETURNS
Upon successful completion, a value of zero is returned. Otherwise, a value of
\-1 is returned and \fIerrno\fR is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The value of the \fIsig\fR argument is invalid. 
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
An attempt was made to catch, ignore, or set SIG_DFL for SIGKILL or SIGSTOP.
.SH SEE ALSO
kill(2),
sigprocmask(2P),
sigsetops(2P),
sigsuspend(2P)
